CODE002 line 15: This line of 4 backticks closes the fence opened with 3; earlier versions kept it as content. To keep it as content, open the fence with more backticks than it has.
CODE003 line 23: This fence opens with 4 backticks and no later line of at least 4 backticks closes it, so it closes at the next "```" line, as in earlier versions. Close it with a line of 4 backticks.
CODE003 line 29: This line has a backtick in its info string, which makes it text in CommonMark; it is read as a fence, as in earlier versions, because as text the lines after it would leave a fence unclosed. Remove the backtick from the info string.
CODE003 line 35: This fence opens with 4 backticks and no later line of at least 4 backticks closes it, so it closes at the next "```" line, as in earlier versions. Close it with a line of 4 backticks.
